{title: 075 - The Wonder of It All}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: God the Father}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]There's the wonder of sunset [F/A]at [F7/A]evening, [Bb]The wonder as [Eb]sunrise I see;
[Eb]But the wonder of [Bb]wonders that thrills my [F7]soul Is the wonder that God loves [D/Gb]me.
[D/Gb]O, the wonder [Gm]of it [Eb]all! The wonder [Bb/F]of it all! Just to think [F]that God [F7]loves [Bb]me.
[F]O, the wonder [Bb]of [F7/A]it all! The [Bb]wonder [Eb]of it all! Just to think that God loves [Bb/F]me.

Refrain:
[F]O, the [F7]wonder of it [Bb]all!
[Bb]The wonder of it all!
[Dm/A]Just to [Bb]think that [F7]God loves [Bb/D]me.
[Eb]O, the wonder of it all!
[Eb]The wonder [Bb/F]of it all!
[F7]Just to think that God loves [Bb]me.

Verse 2:
[Bb]There's the wonder [F7/A]of springtime [Bb/D]and [Eb]harvest,
[Eb]The sky, [Bb]the [F7]stars, the sun;
[D/Gb]But the [Gm]wonder [Eb]of [Bb/F]wonders that [F]thrills [F7]my [Bb]soul
[F]Is the [Bb]wonder that's [Eb]only begun.
